  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: High confidence in impactful heat this week. \n\nThe main storm track remains well north of the area through the\nwork week. A strong mid level ridge will strengthen over the \nArkLaTex, and gradually work its way east, becoming centered \nover the Southern Appalachians by Wednesday into Thursday. \nFriday into the weekend an Omega Block develops, with robust low\npressure over eastern Canada beginning to suppress the ridging \nover the Appalachians.\n\nTemperatures at 850mb will hover around 21-24 degrees C in the \nafternoons and evenings Monday through Thursday. The heat should\npeak Wednesday, but remains quite high Thursday as well, \nespecially over the Piedmont. Temperatures in the 80s and 90s \ncombined with dew points in the mid to upper 60s will result in \nheat indices between 100-106 for parts of the Piedmont as well \nas the Roanoke urban area during this period. It is possible \nheat advisories may be needed; please monitor future updates to \nthe forecast.\n\nThrough Wednesday, and possibly Thursday, rain looks scarce,\nwith a few tiny cells trying to develop in the afternoons and \nearly evenings. We may see a rogue storm develop along the \nsouthern Blue Ridge, but some capping and skinny CAPE will \ncontribute to weaker cells. Higher chances for showers and \nthunderstorms return Friday through Sunday as a cold front nears \nand slowly pushes south across the area, and as the ridge \nweakens.",
